2026-08-10 16:02:12,425 | INFO     | utils.chatbot | │  All Metadata     : {'source': 'uploads\\AIML landscape.pdf', 'page': 0, 'file_type': 'pdf', 'extractor': 'docling', 'original_content': '## INTERNATIONAL AI / MACHINE LEARNING LANDSCAPE\n\nDecember 2016\n\nPrivate and Confidential\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## EU /ISRAEL AI LANDSCAPE KEYFINDINGS\n\n- Magister interviewed 40+ Artificial Intelligence companies across the EU / Israel in a range of application areas, 1 from healthcare to analytics to music production\n- We see the current \'boom\' in Al funding creating significant value due to increased computational capabilities, 2 big data and efficient algorithms\n- Potential Al \'winners\' are all over Europe not just in UK and Israel. Key industries of focus are: Healthcare, 3 Finance, Retail, AdTech/MarTech and Cybersecurity\n- 4 We expect to see 15-20 EU / Israel Al acquisitions in 2017 at valuations as high as $10m per employee\n- 5 We expect an increased interest from mid cap tech and non tech companies following acquisitions by Ford, PTC, 24/7,Quixey\n- In terms of financings, we expect to see a growing number of smaller financing rounds, as Al companies expand 6 incrementally. We do not see huge financing rounds for Al companies as most will be acquired.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## AI HAS EXPERIENCED SEVERAL FALSE DAWNS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDue to lack of progress on machine translation, US govt. ended the support after having spent $20m. It was concluded that "machine translation was more expensive, less accurate and slower than human translation\'\n\n—Automatic Language Processing Advisory Committee\n\n"In no part of the field have discoveries made so far produced the major impact that was then promised. Al techniques may work within the scope of small problem domains, but techniques would not scale up to solve more realistic problems"\n\n—Lighthill report, published by British Science Research Council, that led to funding cuts for most British universities\n\nBefore cutting all the funding. DARPA spent $1B on Strategic Computing Initiative to advance artificial intelligence during 1983-93. "DARPA should focus its funding only on those technologies which showed the most promise"', '_id': '29052cdb-c260-4c27-85dc-fa18948500bb', '_collection_name': 'docmind_green'}
